{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Hierarchical Approximation Chain.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Hierarchical Approximation Chain.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"hierarchical approximation chain hierarchical approximation chain","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Hierarchical Approximation Chain.md","fileName":"Hierarchical Approximation Chain.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Hierarchical Approximation Chain","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 10:19\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Ultrametric Hierarchy and Information]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ultrametric Hierarchy and Information","datasciencefoundations_geometry.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Hierarchical Approximation Chain.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Hierarchical Approximation Chain.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"hierarchical approximation chain hierarchical approximation chain","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Hierarchical Approximation Chain.md","fileName":"Hierarchical Approximation Chain.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Hierarchical Approximation Chain","heading":"Hierarchical Approximation Chain","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A hierarchy can represent one observation as successive approximations. Begin with the global smooth of a dendrogram Haar transform, then add the signed details on that observation's path. Each added branch distinction gives a finer representation until the original vector is recovered.\n\nThe book relates this sequence to a partial order of information: an ancestor-level description is less specific than a descendant-level one. Its simplified face example uses the chain to propose a way to generate an object from a group average and a short sequence of refinements; the practical value depends on the chosen hierarchy and re